meantime dozens of animal rights  activists march for change today  demanding the animal foundation do  better for the animals inside victoria  saha spoke with those rallying and with  staff at the animal foundation  no kill las vegas organized this protest  so they can be the voices for those  animals inside they say enough is enough  and every animal in there deserves to  live protesters gathered at freedom park  and marched their way to the animal  foundation many with signs that say they  want the shelter to stop killing the  animals inside others complained  management issues led to staff quitting  which ultimately leads to the lack of  care for the animals rose gotalero deals  with rescue animals she says she hears  of a lot of them being euthanized there  are an enormous amount of animals that  are being euthanized for not a very good  reason  pertaining to anything from an ear  infection to space issues the animal  foundation acknowledges they have had  staff issues but say they have been  doing better for the past 10 years we  brought our euthanasia rate down by 93  percent so we've dealt with them a  little bit but  we're doing great work ultimately these  protesters want to see someone running  the place that has experience working  with animals and will do their best to  make sure every animal gets a chance to  survive and get adopted reporting from  the animal foundation victoria saha live  local now
 

